/target

# A `.DS_Store` in `projects/` is a real entry that project discovery has to skip, so the
# fixture tree carries one deliberately. Most developers ignore `.DS_Store` globally, and a
# repository `.gitignore` outranks `core.excludesFile`, so this negation is what keeps the
# fixture from being dropped on someone else's machine.
!tests/data/claude/projects/.DS_Store
